      "understanding": {
        "goal_understanding": "The goal was to navigate each level\u2019s grid to step onto and complete all goal cells. A goal cell only counts as completed when my carried piece\u2019s shape, color, and rotation exactly match that goal\u2019s required attributes at the moment I step onto it; completing all goals advances to the next level, and winning all levels completes the game.",
        "mechanics_understanding": "Each move (north/south/east/west) costs 1 stamina; when stamina reaches 0, I lose 1 life and stamina resets to max, and losing all lives ends the game. Movement is constrained by walls: the state provides blocked_directions that must never be chosen because attempting them wastes a turn and stamina without moving. The piece\u2019s attributes are modified by stepping on specific modifier tiles: shape modifiers cycle shape IDs 0\u20135 (wrapping), color modifiers cycle colors in order orange \u2192 blue \u2192 green \u2192 red \u2192 orange, and rotation modifiers rotate 90\u00b0 clockwise (0\u00b0 \u2192 90\u00b0 \u2192 180\u00b0 \u2192 270\u00b0 \u2192 0\u00b0). Once the piece matches a goal\u2019s required shape/color/rotation, the goal becomes activated and is completed by stepping onto that goal cell while still matching."
